tasks/dsh-parity\waves\logs\W5.log-1389-- X7 should connect to the existing DBOS durable backend, `AtlasScheduler`, Hub, Hermes `GoalManager`/`SessionDB` synchronization, and `full_access`/`ask_writes`/`read_only` permission modes. Do not introduce a second runtime, scheduler, goal/session DB, skill registry, or permission engine. [Task 1][Task 2]
tasks/dsh-parity\waves\logs\W5.log-1390-- Windows design boundary: a boot-start noninteractive service handles health/scheduling/recovery, while a per-user interactive worker handles UIA/foreground/browser actions over authenticated local IPC. Worker loss, sleep, lock, offline, and logoff must be durable explicit states; Windows services are noninteractive by default, and `SetThreadExecutionState` cannot override lid closure or user-initiated sleep. [Task 2]
tasks/dsh-parity\waves\logs\W5.log-1391-- Product claims remain vendor claims unless tested. Closed-source dots, Muse, Spark, Grok Bot, Cue, Perplexity Computer, and Claude Cowork are capability references, not reusable source-code sources. [Task 2]
